use ../knowledge/tool-knowledge.flow

context
    Version: 1.3.39-stable

    darwin/amd64 https://acli.atlassian.com/darwin/1.3.39-stable/acli_1.3.39-stable_darwin_amd64.tar.gz
    darwin/arm64 https://acli.atlassian.com/darwin/1.3.39-stable/acli_1.3.39-stable_darwin_arm64.tar.gz
    linux/amd64 https://acli.atlassian.com/linux/1.3.39-stable/acli_1.3.39-stable_linux_amd64.tar.gz
    linux/arm64 https://acli.atlassian.com/linux/1.3.39-stable/acli_1.3.39-stable_linux_arm64.tar.gz
    windows/amd64 https://acli.atlassian.com/windows/1.3.39-stable/acli_1.3.39-stable_windows_amd64.zip
as @atlassian_release

do Resolve the Atlassian CLI version from @options.acli_version when non-null,
    otherwise the Version entry in @atlassian_release. Select its exact URL for
    @platform.os and @platform.arch. For a version override, replace only the
    default version in that URL. Return an object with version and url. as @atlassian_package

print "Step 3 of 3: Set up Atlassian CLI (acli)."

do Probe only @host.acli using @tool_guidance. Match the parsed version exactly to @atlassian_package.version
    and check Jira auth status. Treat missing, broken, or mismatched installations
    as not ready, and missing authentication as false. Return an object with
    path, version, and Boolean ready and authenticated. as @atlassian

if @atlassian.ready is false
    do Download and extract @atlassian_package.url; install at @host.acli using
        @install_rules and @tool_guidance.
        Require @atlassian_package.version. Return an object with path, verified version,
        ready true, and Boolean authenticated from Jira auth status. as @atlassian

if @atlassian.authenticated is false
    print "Complete Jira sign-in in the browser opened by the CLI. Its login URL will be available in the terminal. Keep that terminal open until sign-in finishes."
    do Run @host.acli jira auth login --web in one user-visible interactive
        terminal session using @tool_guidance. Keep that session alive and wait for the process to
        exit successfully; never detach or background it. Then require
        @host.acli jira auth status to succeed. Keep CLI-managed credentials
        without requesting or exposing tokens. If a persistent interactive
        session is unavailable, fail this instruction. Return @atlassian with
        authenticated true. as @atlassian

print Report the verified Atlassian CLI version, path, and Jira authentication state from @atlassian.
